This package bundles and adapts material from GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance
(https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance), Copyright Google LLC,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Bundled without modification:
  - data/guides.json and data/guides/**/*.md — the Modern Web Guidance corpus
    (version 1.0.0, skill version 2026_11_09-5bcc021b). data/guides.json is upstream's
    gen/guides.json, copied unchanged; the guides are the files that index lists. One upstream
    file, data/guides/built-in-ai/prompt-api.md, is not shipped: it is a byte-identical duplicate
    of language-model.md and is absent from the upstream index, so the corpus is 208 files for
    208 index entries (the upstream package itself carries 209 guide files).
  - data/skills/chrome-extensions/** — the Chrome extensions skill
    (skill version 2026_08_06-8570fe7c)

Adapted:
  - data/skills/modern-web-guidance/SKILL.md — rewritten for this plugin: it instructs
    the agent to call the plugin's local tools instead of the upstream `npx` CLI, and it
    drops the upstream CLI workflow and network-approval sections. The guidance content itself
    is unchanged. The file carries an in-header modification notice.
  - Cross-references inside the guide bodies are rewritten at load time, not on disk: the 197
    occurrences of `npx -y modern-web-guidance@latest retrieve "id"` across 64 guides become
    `web_guidance_retrieve({"ids":["id"]})`, so a retrieved guide never tells an agent to fetch and
    execute an unpinned remote package. The markdown files keep matching the pinned upstream
    snapshot byte for byte.

Removed: the upstream `modern-web-guidance` CLI (search.mjs, modern-web.mjs, legacy-scan.mjs and the
TypeScript-based scan engine it embeds), the precomputed semantic-search tables under `gen/`
(query-words.*, guide-chunks.*) and the Google Clearcut telemetry watchdog (`watchdog/`). The 0.x
packages bundled a TensorFlow.js MiniLM embedder instead of those tables; neither is shipped here.
This package performs local lexical search instead and sends no telemetry.
